{# ── Diagnostic & Brand Compatibility E-E-A-T Guide ────────────────────── #}
<div class="rs-choose">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-center" style="max-width:740px;margin-bottom:44px">
      <span class="sub-label" style="background:var(--primary-lt);color:var(--primary);border-color:rgba(37,99,235,0.25)"><i class="ph ph-magnifying-glass" style="font-size:12px"></i> Electrical Safety Guide</span>
      <h2>Common Breaker Symptoms &amp; Supported US Load Centers</h2>
      <p class="sec-desc">Identify why your circuit breaker is tripping before resetting it—and verify the OEM panel brands serviced across the United States.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="diagnostic-grid">
      <div class="diagnostic-card">
        <div class="diag-head">
          <i class="ph ph-warning-octagon" style="color:var(--primary);font-size:20px"></i>
          <h3>Tripping Immediately</h3>
        </div>
        <p><strong>Likely Cause:</strong> Direct short circuit or ground fault in wiring or plugged appliance.</p>
        <p class="diag-action"><strong>Safe Next Step:</strong> Keep the breaker OFF and schedule resistance/short isolation.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="diagnostic-card">
        <div class="diag-head">
          <i class="ph ph-clock-countdown" style="color:var(--primary);font-size:20px"></i>
          <h3>Trips After 10–30 Minutes</h3>
        </div>
        <p><strong>Likely Cause:</strong> Thermal overload from space heaters, AC units, or weakened trip coil.</p>
        <p class="diag-action"><strong>Safe Next Step:</strong> Split heavy appliances or install a dedicated 20A/240V breaker.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="diagnostic-card">
        <div class="diag-head">
          <i class="ph ph-thermometer-hot" style="color:var(--primary);font-size:20px"></i>
          <h3>Buzzing, Warm, or Burnt Smell</h3>
        </div>
        <p><strong>Likely Cause:</strong> Loose terminal lug torque, arcing contact, or pitted bus bar stab.</p>
        <p class="diag-action"><strong>Safe Next Step:</strong> Request same-day thermal inspection and bus bar check.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="diagnostic-card">
        <div class="diag-head">
          <i class="ph ph-shield-check" style="color:var(--primary);font-size:20px"></i>
          <h3>AFCI / GFCI Nuisance Trips</h3>
        </div>
        <p><strong>Likely Cause:</strong> Shared neutral wire, outdoor box moisture, or pinched cable staple.</p>
        <p class="diag-action"><strong>Safe Next Step:</strong> Have a licensed electrician trace ground/arc faults cleanly.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="brand-box">
      <h3><i class="ph ph-plugs-connected" style="color:var(--primary)"></i> UL-Listed US Breaker Brands Serviced &amp; Upgraded</h3>
      <div class="brand-pills">
        <span class="brand-pill">Square D (QO &amp; Homeline)</span>
